[freehsm-c] FATAL : this module is unsigned.
  Its .fhsm_digest section is the all-zero placeholder a fresh
  build leaves, so the integrity self-test has nothing to verify
  against and the module refuses to start (FIPS 140-3 7.10.2).
  If you built it yourself :   make integrity
  If you downloaded it, it was published unsigned -- do not use
  it, and do not set FHSM_INTEGRITY_ALLOW_UNSIGNED to get past
  this. See SECURITY.md, "v1.4.0 published unsigned".
